WEBVTT

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.040
Come on. We don't want to be
caught out here after nightfall.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.840
Blimey! Looks like the old girl
has got the kettle on.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.920
Nice cup o' Rosy Lee.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.520
-LUCY: It's lovely.
-It's merely a trifle, you know.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.880
Still plenty to do.
Ain't quite finished it yet.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.800
It'll look the business
when it is, though.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:42.880
Beaver, is that you?
I've been worried sick!

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.320
If I find you've been
out with Badger again, I...

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.200
Well, those aren't badgers.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:54.720
Oh, I never thought
I'd live to see this day.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.080
Look at my fur. You couldn't
give me ten minutes warning?

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:01.360
I'd have given a week
if I thought it would've helped.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:02.760
(ALL LAUGHING)

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:06.040
Oh, come inside, and we'll see
if we can't get you some food,

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.000
and some civilised company.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.160
(CHUCKLES)

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.920
MR BEAVER: Now, careful.
Watch your step.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.600
MRS BEAVER: Excuse the mess.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.760
Can't get Mr. Beaver
to get out of his chair.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.480
Enjoying the scenery, are we?

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.280
Isn't there anything
we can do to help Tumnus?

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.200
They'll have taken him to the Witch's
house. You know what they say.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:38.120
There's few that go through
them gates that come out again.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.080
Fish 'n' chips?

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:45.440
But there is hope, dear. Lots of hope.

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:48.600
Oh, yeah,
there's a right bit more than hope!

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.920
Aslan is on the move.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:00.880
Who's Aslan?

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:03.120
(LAUGHING) Who's Aslan?

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.080
You cheeky little blighter.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.680
What?

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.640
-You don't know, do you?
-We haven't exactly been here very long.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.480
Well, he's only the king
of the whole wood.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:22.240
The top geezer.
The real King of Narnia.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:25.960
-He's been away for a long while.
-But he's just got back!

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.320
And he's waiting for you
near the Stone Table!

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:31.760
-He's waiting for us?
-You're blooming joking!

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.440
They don't even know
about the prophecy!

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.320
-Well, then...
-Look.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:40.680
Aslan's return,

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:44.080
Tumnus' arrest, the secret police,

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.200
it's all happening because of you!

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:49.680
-You're blaming us?
-No! Not blaming.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:53.000
-Thanking you.
-There's a prophecy.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.600
"When Adam's flesh and Adam's bone

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.760
sits at Cair Paravel in throne,

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:02.280
the evil time will be over and done."

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.880
-That doesn't really rhyme.
-I know it don't.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.400
You're kind of missing the point!

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:09.760
It has long been foretold

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:12.880
that two Sons of Adam
and two Daughters of Eve

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:17.520
will defeat the White Witch
and restore peace to Narnia.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:21.800
And you think we're the ones?

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:24.720
You'd better be, 'cause Aslan's
already fitted out your army.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:27.320
-Our army?
-Mum sent us away

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:30.160
so we wouldn't get caught up in a war.

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:33.440
I think you've made a mistake.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.480
-We're not heroes.
-We're from Finchley.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:41.040
Thank you for your hospitality.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.360
-But we really have to go.
-No, you can't just leave!

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:50.080
He's right.
We have to help Mr. Tumnus.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.080
It's out of our hands.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.200
I'm sorry,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.720
but it's time the four of us
were getting home. Ed?

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.200
Ed?

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:07.120
-I'm gonna kill him.
-MR BEAVER: You may not have to.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.920
Has Edmund ever been
to Narnia before?

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:38.240
Hurry!

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.280
-Edmund!
-They'll hear you!

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:03.760
No!

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:06.240
-Get off me!
-You're playing into her hands.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:08.200
-We can't just let him go!
-He's our brother!

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:10.000
MR BEAVER: He's the bait!

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.320
-The Witch wants all four of you!
-PETER: Why?

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:15.640
To stop the prophecy from coming true.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:17.360
To kill you!

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.200
-This is all your fault.
-My fault?

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:33.400
None of this would have happened
if you had listened to me in the first place!

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:36.240
-You knew this would happen.
-I didn't know.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.400
Which is why we should
have left while we could!

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:39.840
Stop it!

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:44.040
-This isn't going to help Edmund.
-She's right.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:47.840
Only Aslan can help your brother now.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:51.680
Then take us to him.

